TEXT 528 544 Left 2 ;Differential Amplifier with CASCODE Tail (Exercise 6 - Improved CMRR)\n \nDifferential Pair:\n  M1, M2: NMOS (W=20u, L=5u)\n \nActive Load (Current Mirror):\n  M3, M4: PMOS (W=5u, L=5u)\n \nCASCODE Tail Current Source (for high CMRR):\n  MCAS: Upper cascode transistor (W=20u, L=50u)\n  MB: Lower current source (W=20u, L=50u)\n  VBIAS: Sets cascode gate voltage\n  IBIAS: 20µA bias current\n \nOutput Stage:\n  M5: NMOS common-source (W=90u, L=20u)\n \nExpected CMRR Improvement:\n  +20 to 30 dB vs simple tail (Exercise6_Differential_CMRR.asc)\n \nTrade-off:\n  - Better CMRR (higher tail impedance: r_o → g_m*r_o^2)\n  - Loses one V_DSsat of headroom
